<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William II of Württemberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William II of Württemberg was the last King of Württemberg, reigning from 1891 to 1918. A popular and unpretentious constitutional monarch, he ruled his kingdom as a member state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>. He abdicated in November 1918 during the German Revolution, and Württemberg became a republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="William II of Württemberg" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theodor Andersen / Wilhelm Klemm · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andersen_%26_Klemm_-_Wilhelm_II._von_W%C3%BCrttemberg_(1892_RB25-21).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
